# Context is the repo root (frontend/Dockerfile, #2895), and the Dockerfile
# reads only frontend/, NOTICE and LICENSE from it. An ALLOWLIST rather than a
# denylist: the root carries a developer's .env (SECRET_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD),
# .claude/, .charts-render/ and appliance build output, none of which belongs in
# a build context, and a denylist only covers the entries someone remembered.
# BuildKit reads this file in place of a root .dockerignore because it sits
# beside the Dockerfile as <Dockerfile>.dockerignore.
*
!frontend
!NOTICE
!LICENSE

# A developer's local install and build output: npm install in the image
# must not inherit a host node_modules (wrong platform binaries), and dist/
# and dist-legal/ are rebuilt there. frontend/legal is where the Dockerfile
# puts NOTICE and LICENSE; a stale host copy must not shadow the root files.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/dist-legal
frontend/legal
**/.DS_Store
